  "body": "## Problem and change\n\nWith Sequence numbers set to Every block, the Mazak probe macro wrote targets such as `N110 N9001`.\nThe `GOTO9001` branch had no standalone target. Ordinary sequence numbers could also duplicate probe labels.\n\nThe post now records used N numbers in one program-scoped set.\nAutomatic numbers keep the selected start and increment, and skip used numbers.\nProbe labels skip used numbers and are reserved before their numbered branch and alarm blocks.\nThe existing `rawBlock` function writes each standalone label without an automatic prefix.\nThe allocator refuses a nonpositive rounded increment or arithmetic that cannot advance to a finite number.\n\nThe post engine creates a new script context for each program. The set spans sections within that program only.\nDefault output with numbering off remains unchanged. Probe motions, alarm conditions and feeds do not change.\nNo dependency or process file changes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nBase: `NeoTech/Camcraft main 1cf7390dc0acc3248f8e98a6612d6fe6c6001a74`.\nHead: `a34a2e5d8273ccf3d3f5582194bee2cab53b88a5`.\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4342#issuecomment-7229322032\n\n## Reproduction before fix\n\nWindows x64, Rust 1.100.1, four build jobs, `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`.\nThe tests post the existing `recorded/inputs/probe_t7_bore_g55.cnc` stream through `engine::run_with`.\nThe production implementation stayed unchanged at the exact base above for this reading.\n\n```text\ncargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_probe mazak_sequence_labels:: -- --nocapture\n```\n\nAt this stage the module held the three original regression tests. All three failed: 0 passed, 3 failed, exit 101.\nThe cold build took 11 min 39 s. The tests took 0.17 s.\n\n- `every_block_probe_labels_are_unambiguous_jump_targets`: `GOTO9001` had zero standalone `N9001` targets. The actual line was `N110 N9001`.\n- `probe_labels_never_collide_with_numbered_blocks`: start 1 and increment 1000 emitted `N9001` more than once.\n- `probe_labels_remain_unique_across_sections_and_word_spacing`: the two-section program also duplicated `N9001`.\n\nThe three assertions remain unchanged. The final module adds the golden and invalid-option tests below.\nTo repeat the baseline, copy the final test module and registration into an isolated worktree at the base.\nRun each of the three original test names with\n`cargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_probe mazak_sequence_labels::<name> -- --exact --nocapture`.\n\n## After fix and final-head checks\n\nThe five tests in `mazak_sequence_labels` pass. The complete `script_probe` suite passes 44 tests.\nThe new cases cover all numbering modes, start 1/increment 1000, starts 8999/9000/9001,\nthe declared maximum start 999999/increment 10000, two sections, and word spacing on and off.\nRaw nonadvancing numeric options are refused by name.\n\nPinning tests in the existing `script_probe` directory suite:\n\n- `mazak_sequence_labels::every_block_probe_labels_are_unambiguous_jump_targets`\n- `mazak_sequence_labels::probe_labels_never_collide_with_numbered_blocks`\n- `mazak_sequence_labels::probe_labels_remain_unique_across_sections_and_word_spacing`\n- `mazak_sequence_labels::nonadvancing_sequence_options_are_refused_by_name`\n- `mazak_sequence_labels::every_block_probe_matches_its_golden`\n\nThe final-head post checks pass: 1,418 tests across ten targets.\n\n| Target | Passed |\n| --- | ---: |\n| lib | 184 |\n| post_engine | 143 |\n| script_arcs | 49 |\n| script_cycles | 122 |\n| script_dialects | 175 |\n| script_edm | 87 |\n| script_goldens | 440 |\n| script_probe | 44 |\n| script_rotary | 66 |\n| script_wcs | 108 |\n\nThe commands were `cargo test -j4 -p camcraft-post --lib`, then\n`cargo test -j4 -p camcraft-post --test <target>` for each named integration binary.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` passes in 1 min 50 s.\n\nValidation uses the touched-binary and strict-clippy alternative in `work-issue` section 3.\nThe quick dry run selects 42 steps. The ten directly affected post targets ran as above.\nThe 21 other app suites and two prebuild steps did not run through that full quick plan.\n\nThe nine required app example suites pass: 80 tests passed, with four existing heavy tests ignored.\nEach ran with `cargo test -j4 -p camcraft-app --test <target>`:\n\n- `example_catalog`\n- `example_catalog_adaptive`\n- `example_catalog_edge_work`\n- `first_part_programs`\n- `first_router_part`\n- `first_4axis_part`\n- `continuous_4axis_part`\n- `tilt_basis_compat`\n- `catalog_groove_part_off`\n\nAll 11 light twins pass in release mode with this command:\n\n```text\ncargo xtask gate light --only 'motion light:' --only 'app light:'\n```\n\nThe selected plan ran five of six steps, with zero failed or stalled steps.\nIt includes seven motion lib twins, one each in `adaptive_troch_island`,\n`adaptive_troch_neck` and `adaptive_troch_parallel`, and one app `pocket_pass_start` twin.\nOnly the generic, unfiltered release `--no-run` prebuild is omitted.\nThe cold light run took 32.6 minutes.\n\nThe final checks total 1,509 passed tests. The complete quick plan and full heavy lane did not run.\n\n## Files and golden\n\n- `assets/posts/mazak.cps`: shared N-number allocation and standalone probe targets.\n- `crates/post/tests/script_probe/main.rs`: register the test module.\n- `crates/post/tests/script_probe/mazak_sequence_labels.rs`: five focused tests.\n- `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/mazak/probe_every_block.nc`: one new Every block probe golden.\n- `docs/decisions/4342-mazak-probe-sequence.md`: allocation choice and rejected alternatives.\n\nGoldens moved: one addition only. No existing golden changes.\nThe new golden has 13 standalone targets, `N9001` through `N9013`, with ordinary numbers from `N10` through `N790`.\n\n## Merge interaction and limits\n\nAt this draft's preparation, PR #4413 is open and draft at `e33fc70b9066c9e8e77c94f1d0dfa8e3fb34a398`.\nPR #4371 is also open and draft at `ce23fdaa8`.\nThey change the Mazak feed-mode preamble and retract logic. This fix changes independent functions.\n\nThe PR that merges second between this fix and #4413 must regenerate the new special-option golden with G94.\nSet `WRITE_GOLDEN=1` for this one command, then restore or unset it:\n\n```text\ncargo test -p camcraft-post --test script_probe mazak_sequence_labels::every_block_probe_matches_its_golden -- --exact\n```\n\nNo physical Mazak control, full heavy lane or release gate was tested.\nThis contributor PR leaves maintainer review and merge control unchanged.\n\nChangelog: Mazak probing writes unique standalone jump labels when sequence numbers are enabled, so alarm branches find their targets.\n\nFixes #4342\n",
